(* Variant quic-nocert-none: a QUIC client that got no certificate of the server (no
   QUIC_CONNECTION_EVENT_PEER_CERTIFICATE_RECEIVED), against an attacker that is the network (AUD-6, #409). Each side runs
   the session bound or encrypted from what its own transport gives it (TransportNoiseStart): this client has no
   tls-server-end-point, so QuicStreamBinding gives it none, it checks no pin and runs an encrypted session with the
   prologue of no binding, while the server, which knows its certificate, runs a bound one. The two prologues differ, so
   the handshake cannot complete, which reach-took and reach-done must prove. The model has the handshake of such a
   client, not the records under the Noise keys that it would send after one. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | Sessions(pin_off, bt_none, bt_endpoint, kp_on, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
